    "result": "I implemented both functions in `solution.py` and wrote 27 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py`; `python -m pytest -q tests` passes all of them. `can_book` checks the rules in spec order: it raises `ValueError` for `end <= start` or a negative buffer, then rejects bookings that cross a calendar day, exceed 4 hours, or fall outside `open_time`–`close_time`, with boundaries inclusive. For conflicts it applies the buffer symmetrically, so with `b = 0` back-to-back bookings are allowed and with `b > 0` they need at least `b` minutes of gap. `merge_intervals` validates every interval, sorts a new list by start, and merges overlapping or touching pairs without modifying the input. I only edited `solution.py` and files under `tests/`, and I created no other files.",
